    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32097" root="غفر" body-key="g">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تغفّر</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَغْفَرَ</span></b>  <i>He gathered what is called</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِغْفَر</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغْفُور</span> [see the latter of these two words].
(S, K.) He who says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغْفُور</span> says ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرَجْنَا نَتَمَغْفَرُ</span></b> ,
and he who says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِغْفَر</span> says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خرجنا نَتَغَفَّرُ</span>, <i>We went
forth to gather</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مغفور</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مغفر</span>, <i>from its trees.</i> (S.)

